      "problem": "Write $0.\\overline{23}$ as geometric series.",
      "worked_solution": "The given repeating decimal can be written as \n\n$$\n0.\\overline{23} = 0.23 + 0.002\\,3 + 0.000\\,023 + \\dots\n$$\n\n$$\n0.\\overline{23} = \\dfrac{23}{100} + \\dfrac{23}{10\\,000} + \\dfrac{23}{1\\,000\\,000}+\\dots\n$$\n\nwhere the first term is $a_1 = \\dfrac{23}{100}$ and the common ratio is $\\dfrac{1}{100}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.\\overset{―}{23} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{23}{100}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }23\\cdot \\frac{1}{100}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }23\\cdot \\frac{1}{100}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{100})}^{-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }23{(\\frac{1}{100})}^{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
